Modifications made for pi (none of these exist upstream):

- office              : the "skill" tool invocation is replaced by reading the
                        sibling skill's SKILL.md, because pi loads skills by
                        reading files instead of calling a skill tool.
- office-docx/-xlsx/-pptx : "load_workspace_dependencies" is replaced by the
                        python/SETUP.md consent-first environment procedure.
- office-render/-recalculate/-export-pdf : node and CLI paths injected at load
                        time upstream are replaced by scripts/resolve-dsoffice.mjs,
                        which resolves them at runtime.
- delivery via "present" is replaced by reporting the final file path, since pi
  has no present tool.
- skills/office/references/sidecar.md is rewritten for npm-installed
  dependencies (upstream describes a DSH-native bootstrap).
- python/SETUP.md, python/requirements.txt and scripts/resolve-dsoffice.mjs are
  new files written for this port.
- scripts/sync-from-dsh.mjs and upstream.json are new files that re-port the
  skill texts from a published upstream version and fail loudly when upstream
  wording drifts (see README, "Keeping up with upstream").

